Good morning,

We are instructed to notify the total loss by fire of a scheduled excavator belonging to our client Ironbark Constructors, Inc. Our reference is SRR/IM/2025/2298.

Policy number: IM-2298-66401
Insured name: Ironbark Constructors, Inc.
Scheduled item: Item 001, Caterpillar 349, serial CAT0349FKMBX2117
Date of loss: 14 November 2025
Loss location: Interstate 10 westbound, milepost 168, near Casa Grande, AZ
Cause: Fire - hydraulic line failure onto the exhaust
Estimated loss: USD 715,950

The machine was on our client's own lowboy moving between their Mesa yard and a
job in Buckeye. The driver saw smoke, pulled over, and found flame at the
turbocharger. Casa Grande Fire attended. It is a constructive total loss. No
injuries and no other vehicles involved.

The lowboy trailer itself and the ADOT highway damage are motor vehicle exposures
and are excluded from this floater under the licensed highway vehicle exclusion.
We are presenting those to the commercial auto carrier separately.

The machine has not been touched. It is tarped in the client's Phoenix yard and
the suspect hydraulic line is still in place in the burned compartment.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * equipment assessor's report
  * equipment loss schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an assessor. A substitute machine was hired
from 18 November, so rental reimbursement is running.

